        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: выпускник",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "выпускник (vypuskník) — \"a school-leaver, a graduate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Выпускники подарили учителю цветы. Vypusknikí podaríli uchítelyu tsvetý. The school-leavers gave the teacher flowers."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A woman is выпускница."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "выпускник (vypuskník) is built on выпуск \"a graduating class\", from выпускать \"to let out\", whose root is Proto-Slavic pustiti \"to let go\" (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
